# tfpp-glm: this node's own values (bash, sourced by start_stage.sh / stop_stage.sh). Copy to node.env on each N1X
# and keep exactly one block. Chain C -> A -> B (spec 2.2); the layer cuts are the recommended ones.
#   s0 = C (the 64 GB node, ~38 GiB)  --USB4 subnet 1-->  s1 = A (~92 GiB, two USB4 ports)  --USB4 subnet 2-->  leader = B
# Each inbound hop reaches WSL through relay_hop.ps1 on the receiving node's Windows side (A, B). Stage 0 needs none.
# Start in any order (a follower retries until the next stage answers, through this relay_hop.ps1 too); stop the
# leader only (QUIT ends the chain).

# ---- s0: C (the 64 GB node), layers [0, 7) ------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROLE=follower
LAYERS=0:7
MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/glm53                # config.json, tokenizer.json, model.safetensors.index.json, shards 2-10
DOWN=10.77.0.2:5301                         # A's relay (A's USB4 address on subnet 1)
RESERVE_GIB=2.5
PREFETCH_NEXT=0                             # one layer in flight: the 64 GB node's host memory is tight
TFPP_WARM_MS=1.0
# stop other GPU workloads on this node first; start_stage.sh refuses to start beside a listener on one of
# GPU_GUARD_PORTS (below) unless ALLOW_GPU_SHARING=1

# ---- s1: A, layers [7, 26) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROLE=follower
# LAYERS=7:26
# MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/glm53             # shards 10-45
# LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5301                      # inside WSL; relay_hop.ps1 forwards 10.77.0.2:5301 here
# DOWN=10.78.0.2:5302                      # B's relay (subnet 2)
# RESERVE_GIB=3
# PREFETCH_NEXT=1
# TFPP_WARM_MS=1.0

# ---- leader: B, layers [26, 45) + norm + head + embed + DFlash2 + vision + HTTP ---------------------------------
# ROLE=leader
# LAYERS=26:45
# MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/glm53             # shards 1, 2, 45-80, 82, 83 (vision); 81 too for MTP at P=1
# DRAFTER_DIR=$HOME/models/glm53-dflash2   # incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2@bf582e4e (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, optional:
#                                          # NO_DRAFTS=1 runs without it): config.json + model.safetensors
# LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5302                      # relay_hop.ps1 forwards 10.78.0.2:5302 here
# RESERVE_GIB=3
# TF_GLM_CACHE_GIB=6.2                     # kept prompts (the leader's bytes; only the leader reads it)
# TFPP_WARM_MS=1.0
# NO_DRAFTS=0
# TRACE=                                   # a JSONL path: trace every request (tests)

# ---- any node, optional ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUDGET_GIB=                              # the caches' budget outright: required when stages share one GPU
# GPU_GUARD_PORTS=                         # ports other GPU servers on this node listen on, e.g. "8000":
#                                          # start_stage.sh refuses to start while one of them is in use
# ALLOW_GPU_SHARING=0                      # 1: start beside another GPU workload anyway
# VERIFY_SHARDS=0                          # 1: check this stage's shards against their Hub sha256 (cached)
# T2 (a shortened model over two machines, spec 13.1): on the leader TRUNCATE=24 TAP_LAYERS=5,9,14,18,22
#   BENCH=$HOME/hive-ram/tfpp/tfpp/glm/bench_prompts.jsonl TRACE=$HOME/t2.jsonl (no HTTP; ends with QUIT);
#   (paths: your checkout) the 128 GB node runs s1 and the leader: BUDGET_GIB on both; for a bit-equal trace
#   against that node's one-process run
#   keep the kept-prompt byte cap out of play on both sides (TF_GLM_CACHE_GIB=8 and a BUDGET_GIB whose room holds
#   it: run_truncated.sh's header), since which states a byte cap evicts depends on the cut
# TFPP_GLM_VENV=$HOME/tf-venv-mia           # the MIA package's venv (tf-venv-061 stays the Flash-Next one)
# TFPP_GLM_TF_ROOT=                         # instead of a venv copy: a folder holding tensorfold/ (PYTHONPATH overlay)

# ---- tfpp-glm v2: --parallel 2..8 (spec v2; the leader's node.env; the followers take P, the pool and the rest from GO / AGREE) ----
# Only for PARALLEL > 1; with these keys unset the commands are v1's. cluster.env keeps PARALLEL=1 until M6.3's numbers are in.
# PARALLEL=4                               # concurrent streams (v2.0: one round on the chain at a time, see IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md)
# POOL_ROWS=                               # tests: the pool's tokens on every stage (a multiple of 2048), pins the pool plan
# KEPT_ENTRIES=                            # tests: kept prompt states, pins the count
# MBENCH=$HOME/hive-ram/tfpp/tfpp/glm/schedules/AS2.json   # a lockstep / free schedule instead of HTTP (BENCH_OUT: its replies)
# TFPP_GLM_TIMING=1                        # any stage: a log line every 100 rounds (ms a round, ms of it waiting for the stage before)
# TFPP_GLM_TIME_ROWS=1                     # any stage: the batched verify window's ms by rows 1..32, after its graphs are captured
# TFPP_GLM_FAULT_V2=round.act:3            # leader, tests: raise the 3rd time at round.windows|round.act|round.keeps|fill.sent|admit.after
# TFPP_GLM_FAULT_FOLLOWER=windows:40       # follower, tests: SIGKILL itself the 40th time at windows|act
